                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                        "entry_id": "25e11a9f-d638-35a3-8032-78f00b6f8632",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a rapport aux microbes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6738eb4e-cdc6-4802-8482-a66cc942ced3",
                                "sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                                "text": "Aujourd’hui peu peuplée, la forêt a perdu la majorité de sa population humaine sous le choc microbien de la colonisation européenne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78d43dd0-9ccf-4b9a-a6b6-efab35b009c6",
                                "sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                                "text": "Aux États-Unis, les efforts de l’administration Trump pour affranchir les industries extractives et l’ensemble des activités industrielles de toute réglementation ne pourront manquer d’aggraver la perte des habitats, favorisant le transfert microbien des animaux aux humains."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c44fef1e-0c29-40cb-a254-9f6b677cc959",
                                "sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                                "text": "Les composés chimiques ci-dessus indiqués sont des microbicides de degré variable: il n'y a dès lors rien d'étonnant à leur voir suspendre ou arrêter définitivement le processus germinatif, suivant leur degré de nocuité sur la vie microbienne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bf70186-8cca-4e94-83ff-0e3ced4633e7",
                                "sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                                "text": "La région du Sahel est soumise à de très fortes variations de pluviométrie, surtout lors du passage de la saison sèche à la saison humide. Ces variations modifient directement l’humidité des sols et par conséquent l’activité microbienne responsable des émissions de composés azotés [notamment d’oxyde d’azote (NO), de protoxyde d’azote (N₂O) et d’ammoniaque (NH₃) via des processus de minéralisation et de nitrification/dénitrification] et de dioxyde de carbone (CO₂) (respiration microbienne à l’issue de la décomposition de la matière organique)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0da87024-fe2f-42e0-9603-9b2b87a0ced2",
                        "source_entry_id": "25e11a9f-d638-35a3-8032-78f00b6f8632",
                        "source_sense_id": "8b119cad-b071-3621-8135-71773e6583f2",
                        "target_lang_word": "microbial",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "microbial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64199e6f-f641-3fb9-af0b-c2f2ba8f4fa1",
                                        "entry_id": "6c2599db-875d-3c4e-bb66-2fc309f2047f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or caused by microbes or microorganisms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbd6420a-2bd3-432c-8f93-c02efba5e871",
                                                "sense_id": "64199e6f-f641-3fb9-af0b-c2f2ba8f4fa1",
                                                "text": "The close analogies between DNA-containing eukaryotic cell organelles and microbial symbionts require revision of classic cell theory, wrote Scwemmler and Schenk (1980) on introducing the field of endocytobiology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "719a1e2d-8f19-429f-8d6a-c9e2d6d45409",
                                                "sense_id": "64199e6f-f641-3fb9-af0b-c2f2ba8f4fa1",
                                                "text": "Many genes with reproductive roles also have antibacterial and immune functions, which indicate that the threat of microbial attack on the sperm or egg may be a major influence on rapid evolution during reproduction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39ad2fd5-d239-3574-ab12-459bd25b6806",
                                        "entry_id": "6c2599db-875d-3c4e-bb66-2fc309f2047f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small; tiny; minuscule."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5611ff66-c17a-4dab-8915-7f0b318efaca",
                                                "sense_id": "39ad2fd5-d239-3574-ab12-459bd25b6806",
                                                "text": "As I say, one must not blame the Christians too much for all this - partly because, after the communal periods which I have just mentioned, Christianity was evidently deeply influenced by the rise of Commercialism to which during the last two centuries it has so carefully and piously adapted itself; and partly because - if our view is anywhere near right - this microbial injection of self-consciousness was just the necessary work which (in conjunction with commercialism) it had to perform."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
